{"id":"evt_169ed2ac1001W9J2l7quFvsX76","created":1792778513089,"type":"session.reasoning.ended","location":{"directory":"/home/tim/voice-agent/tool/testlab"},"data":{"sessionID":"ses_e9612e73dffeZdaxuXZj1TcFJx","assistantMessageID":"msg_169ed26600015aPJliYtMe7II4","ordinal":0,"text":"According to the global instructions, commands that could potentially take more than about 15 seconds must not be awaited directly. sleep 25 takes 25 seconds. It should be launched detached with nohup and polled, or alternatively a longer timeout could be set. The instructions say to launch it detached and poll with tail. Let's follow that: run `nohup sleep 25 > /tmp/opencode-sleep.log 2>&1 &`, echo the PID, then poll.\n\nActually, sleep doesn't produce any output. But I'll follow the pattern: launch detached, poll with kill -0. Let's run it detached and wait/poll with short calls.\n","state":{"reasoningField":"reasoning_content"}},"durable":{"aggregateID":"ses_e9612e73dffeZdaxuXZj1TcFJx","seq":53,"version":1}}
